<p>You can use the optional folding unit to fold your prints as they come 
 out.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, this function may not be available.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If the <span class="Term-Soft">Fold:</span> list 
 is grayed out, check that the optional folding unit is installed on the 
 printer and selected on the <span class="Term-Soft">Accessories</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Available fold type changes according to paper 
 orientation, 2 sided setting, and stapling position.</p></li>
<li><p>The folding function is not available for certain 
 paper sizes and media types. For details, see the operating instructions 
 provided with the printer.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Finishing</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the fold type in the <span class="Term-Soft">Fold:</span> 
 list.</p></li>
<li><p>If necessary, select the <span class="Term-Soft">Multi-sheet 
 Fold</span> check box.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Depending on 
 the combination of fold type and print side that you have selected, this 
 function might not be available.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="5">
<li><p>After making any additional settings, click <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
